></span></span>Amazon Bedrock<span class="text-caption text-secondary col-start-2">InvokeModel</span><span class="sr-only">Available</span></span></span><span class="flex flex-col gap-xs"><span class="grid items-center gap-x-xs grid-cols-[auto_1fr]"><span class="inline-flex" title="Available"><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" class="shrink-0 text-success" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>Claude Models on Google Cloud<span class="text-caption text-secondary col-start-2">Google managed</span><span class="sr-only">Available</span></span></span><span class="flex flex-col gap-xs"><span class="grid items-center gap-x-xs grid-cols-[auto_1fr]"><span class="inline-flex" title="Available"><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" class="shrink-0 text-success" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>Microsoft Foundry<span class="sr-only">Available</span></span></span></dd></div><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-xs"><dt class="text-caption text-muted"><a href="#feature-beta-headers" class="cds-reset cds-text-link cds-text-link-underline inline text-inherit [transition-property:text-decoration-color,box-shadow] [&amp;:not(:hover,:focus-visible)]:[--_text-link-line:color-mix(in_srgb,currentColor,transparent_35%)] cursor-pointer" data-inherit-color="" data-cds="TextLink">Beta header</a></dt><dd class="flex flex-col items-start gap-xs text-footnote text-primary wrap-anywhere"><span class="">Varies; see details</span></dd></div><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-xs"><dt class="text-caption text-muted"><a href="#feature-data-handling" class="cds-reset cds-text-link cds-text-link-underline inline text-inherit [transition-property:text-decoration-color,box-shadow] [&amp;:not(:hover,:focus-visible)]:[--_text-link-line:color-mix(in_srgb,currentColor,transparent_35%)] cursor-pointer" data-inherit-color="" data-cds="TextLink">Data handling</a></dt><dd class="flex flex-col items-start gap-xs text-footnote text-primary wrap-anywhere"><span class="flex flex-col gap-xs"><span class="grid items-center gap-x-xs grid-cols-[auto_1fr]"><span class="inline-flex"><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" class="shrink-0 text-success" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>ZDR eligible</span></span><span class="flex flex-col gap-xs"><span class="grid items-center gap-x-xs grid-cols-[auto_1fr]"><span class="inline-flex"><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" class="shrink-0 text-success" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>HIPAA eligible</span></span></dd></div></dl></div></div></aside></div><aside data-cds="Aside" data-prose-box="" data-icon-layout="first-line" role="note" class="flex items-start gap-xs rounded-card px-lg py-md font-sans text-body font-normal break-words bg-surface-1 layers-1-[color:var(--cds-banner-neutral-tint)] text-primary shadow-[inset_0_0_0_var(--cds-ring-inner)_var(--cds-banner-neutral-ring,var(--cds-ring-color)),0_0_0_var(--cds-ring-outer)_var(--cds-banner-neutral-ring,var(--cds-ring-color))] [--cds-prose-code-color:initial] [--cds-prose-marker-color:var(--cds-text-secondary)] [--cds-text-link-color:initial] prose-block print:break-inside-avoid print:[:is(h2,h3,h4)+&amp;]:break-after-avoid"><span class="flex min-h-[1lh] shrink-0 items-center"><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:433.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><div class="min-w-0 flex-1"><p><strong>Start with the SDK toolsets:</strong> For <code>computer_toolset_20260801</code>, the Python and TypeScript SDKs have a computer toolset class, in beta. Start from <a href="/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/browser-use-sdk#partner-integrations">a partner’s integration</a>, or see the <a href="/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/browser-use-sdk#computer-toolset">computer toolset</a> section of the SDK toolsets page. Use this page as the tool reference, or when you handle the tool calls yourself.</p></div></aside>
<p>Claude can interact with computer environments through the computer use tool, which provides screenshot capabilities and mouse/keyboard control for autonomous desktop interaction.</p>
<p>The computer use tool is an Anthropic-defined <a href="/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/tool-reference#client-toolsets">client toolset</a>: one <code>{&quot;type&quot;: &quot;computer_toolset_20260801&quot;}</code> entry in <code>tools</code> gives Claude 17 member tools such as <code>screenshot</code>, <code>left_click</code>, <code>type</code>, and <code>zoom</code>, and your application runs every call in an environment you control. It isn’t currently available in <a href="/docs/en/managed-agents/tools">Claude Managed Agents</a>. Claude’s calls are <code>tool_use</code> blocks whose <code>name</code> is the member and which carry <code>&quot;toolset_name&quot;: &quot;computer&quot;</code>, often several in one turn (a <a href="#batch-actions">batch action</a>).</p>
<p>For tasks that stay inside webpages, the <a href="/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/browser-use-tool">browser use tool</a> is the closer fit: its member tools read and act on the page itself, and it doesn’t need a full desktop environment.</p>
<p>See <a href="#availability-feature-support">API support</a> for the models and platforms that support the toolset. <a href="#earlier-tool-versions">Earlier tool versions</a> lists each earlier version’s beta header and the models to use it with.</p>
<h2 id="security-considerations" class="group">Security considerations<span class="relative hidden h-[1em] w-0 align-middle lg:inline-block"><span role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></span><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 data-[copied]:opacity-100 touch:opacity-100" aria-label="Copy link to Security considerations" id="_R_182vcqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h2>
<p>Computer use has unique risks distinct from standard API features. These risks are heightened when interacting with the internet.</p>
<aside data-cds="Aside" data-prose-box="" data-icon-layout="first-line" role="note" class="flex items-start gap-xs rounded-card px-lg py-md font-sans text-body font-normal break-words bg-warning text-warning shadow-ring-warning [--cds-prose-code-color:currentColor] [--cds-prose-marker-color:currentColor] [--cds-text-link-color:var(--cds-text-warning)] stacks:bg-page stacks:layers-1-warning stacks:shadow-none prose-block print:break-inside-avoid print:[:is(h2,h3,h4)+&amp;]:break-after-avoid"><span class="flex min-h-[1lh] shrink-0 items-center"><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:433.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><div class="min-w-0 flex-1"><p>To minimize risks, consider taking precautions such as:</p><ol>
<li>Using a dedicated virtual machine or container with minimal privileges to prevent direct system attacks or accidents.</li>
<li>Avoiding giving the model access to sensitive data, such as account login information, to prevent information theft.</li>
<li>Limiting internet access to an allowlist of domains to reduce exposure to malicious content.</li>
<li>Asking a human to confirm decisions that might result in meaningful real-world consequences and any tasks requiring affirmative consent, such as accepting cookies, completing financial transactions, or agreeing to terms of service.</li>
</ol></div></aside>
<p>In some circumstances, Claude follows commands found in content even when they conflict with your instructions. For example, instructions on webpages or contained in images might override your instructions or cause Claude to make mistakes. Take precautions to isolate Claude from sensitive data and actions to avoid risks related to prompt injection.</p>
<p>Anthropic has trained the model to resist these prompt injections and has added an extra layer of defense. If you use the computer use tool, classifiers automatically scan what the tool returns, such as screenshots, to flag potential prompt injections. When these classifiers identify a potential prompt injection, they steer the model to check whether the instruction really came from you before acting on it.</p>
<p>This extra protection isn’t ideal for every use case (for example, use cases without a human in the loop), so if you’d like to opt out and turn it off, <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">contact support</a>. The precautions listed earlier remain important even with these classifiers in place.</p>
<p>Inform end users of relevant risks and obtain their consent prior to enabling computer use in your own products.</p>
<h2 id="quick-start" class="group">Quick start<span class="relative hidden h-[1em] w-0 align-middle lg:inline-block"><span role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></span><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 data-[copied]:opacity-100 touch:opacity-100" aria-label="Copy link to Quick start" id="_R_186fcqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h2>
<p>Add the computer use toolset to the <code>tools</code> array of a <a id="_R_4g6vcqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" aria-describedby="_R_2sg6vcqalubtabsknr5td9leailbH1_" href="/docs/en/api/messages/create">Messages API</a><span id="_R_2sg6vcqalubtabsknr5td9leailbH1_" data-find-omitted="" class="sr-only select-none">Preview with links to the API reference available — press Tab until focus enters the card, Escape to return.</span> request as <code>{&quot;type&quot;: &quot;computer_toolset_20260801&quot;}</code>. The request needs no beta header. This example also declares the <a href="/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/text-editor-tool">text editor tool</a> and <a href="/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/bash-tool">bash tool</a>, which Claude typically uses alongside computer use:</p>
