<h2 id="migrate-from-computer-20251124" class="group">Migrate from <code>computer_20251124</code><span class="relative hidden h-[1em] w-0 align-middle lg:inline-block"><span role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></span><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 data-[copied]:opacity-100 touch:opacity-100" aria-label="Copy link to Migrate from computer_20251124" id="_R_19lvcqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h2>
<p>A <code>computer_20251124</code> integration works without changes on the models listed for that version under <a href="#earlier-tool-versions">Earlier tool versions</a>. Upgrade the integration before you move it to a model that doesn’t accept <code>computer_20251124</code>, such as a Claude 5.5 model on the Claude API.</p>
<p>To upgrade, make the following changes together:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Remove the beta header.</strong> Drop <code>anthropic-beta: computer-use-2025-11-24</code> from your requests. With the SDK, remove <code>betas</code> and call the Messages API through the standard client rather than the beta namespace.</li>
<li><strong>Change the <code>tools</code> entry.</strong> Set <code>type</code> to <code>computer_toolset_20260801</code> and delete <code>name</code>, <code>display_width_px</code>, <code>display_height_px</code>, <code>display_number</code>, and <code>enable_zoom</code>. The toolset rejects each of these fields.</li>
<li><strong>Choose whether to keep zoom enabled.</strong> Zoom is enabled by default on the toolset, whereas <code>enable_zoom</code> defaults to <code>false</code>. If your environment doesn’t implement zoom, add <code>&quot;configs&quot;: {&quot;zoom&quot;: {&quot;enabled&quot;: false}}</code> to keep the previous behavior; otherwise implement it (see <a href="#available-actions">Available actions</a>).</li>
<li><strong>Handle every block in a turn.</strong> Update your agent loop to iterate over every <code>tool_use</code> block in a response rather than reading only the first, and to dispatch on the block’s <code>name</code> together with <code>toolset_name</code> instead of on <code>input.action</code>. Member inputs no longer contain an <code>action</code> field; the remaining fields are unchanged.</li>
<li><strong>Run blocks in order and use the halt text.</strong> Run the blocks sequentially, stop at the first failure, and answer the remaining blocks with <code>Not executed: an earlier computer action in this turn failed.</code> as described in <a href="#batch-actions">Batch actions</a>. If your loop can’t run batches yet, <a href="#tool-parameters">Tool parameters</a> explains how to limit Claude to one action for each turn.</li>
<li><strong>Echo <code>toolset_name</code> on results.</strong> Add <code>&quot;toolset_name&quot;: &quot;computer&quot;</code> to every <code>tool_result</code> that answers a member call. Results may contain only <code>text</code> and <code>image</code> content.</li>
<li><strong>Support <code>repeat</code> on <code>key</code>.</strong> The <code>key</code> member accepts an optional <code>repeat</code> count from 1 to 100. A handler that ignores unrecognized fields would press the key once, so make your <code>key</code> handler honor <code>repeat</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Resize screenshots yourself.</strong> The toolset rejects a screenshot or zoom image that exceeds the model’s image limits instead of downscaling it. Resize before returning the image and keep scaling coordinates as described in <a href="#handle-coordinate-scaling-for-higher-resolutions">Size screenshots to fit image limits</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Remove unsupported options.</strong> Move any <code>defer_loading</code> from the entry into <code>configs</code>, with the same value on every enabled member. The other options not supported on toolset entries are listed under <a href="/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/tool-reference#client-toolsets">Client toolsets</a>.</li>
</ol>
<p>This is the <code>tools</code> entry before the change, sent with the <code>anthropic-beta: computer-use-2025-11-24</code> header:</p>
